  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P0] Return the declared `id` field instead of `userId`",
      "body": "The changed line returns an object that cannot satisfy the declared return type. `User` requires `id: string` and has no `userId` property, so under standard TypeScript type-checking this file fails to compile regardless of configuration: missing required property `id` (TS2741) and excess property `userId` on the literal (TS2353) — missing-property errors are unconditional, not strictness-dependent. Even if type errors were bypassed by a transpile-only pipeline, every successful `loadUser` call would return a shape violating its exported contract, leaving `user.id` `undefined` for all consumers. This also contradicts the PR's stated intent of \"preserving existing contracts.\" Fix by restoring `id: row.id`, or — if the rename is intentional — updating `export type User` (and any consumers) in the same change.",
      "severity": "P0",
